import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro'; import Breadcrumbs from '../components/Breadcrumbs.astro'; import CallToAction from '../components/CallToAction.astro';
---
<BaseLayout title="How FM AI Assistent Works with FM26 Data" description="Understand how FM AI Assistent reads a user-triggered RAM snapshot, stores it locally and supplies optional context to an AI provider." path="/how-it-works/">
  <div class="page-shell"><Breadcrumbs items={[{label:'How it works'}]} /><header class="page-hero"><p class="eyebrow">The data path</p><h1>How FM AI Assistent works.</h1><p class="lead">The app reads data available in your running FM26 process when you load or refresh it. That local snapshot powers searches and analysis—it is not a continuously synchronized cloud copy.</p></header>
    <section class="section"><div class="steps"><article class="step"><h3>FM26 is running</h3><p>Open a save and run both programs as the same computer user.</p></article><article class="step"><h3>You trigger a load</h3><p>Select <strong>Load data</strong> in the app when you want a fresh snapshot.</p></article><article class="step"><h3>The snapshot commits</h3><p>Player, staff, club and competition readers run concurrently; completed results commit atomically.</p></article><article class="step"><h3>You explore or ask</h3><p>Browse locally or allow a selected AI provider to call focused tools.</p></article></div></section>
    <section class="section feature-showcase"><div><p class="eyebrow">Snapshot, not stream</p><h2>Freshness stays under your control.</h2><p>After switching saves, changing clubs or advancing to information you want updated, select <strong>Load data</strong> again. The app can also expose snapshot status and let an authorized agent request a refresh.</p><p>If a reader or local database write fails, the previous complete snapshot remains available rather than exposing a half-refreshed dataset.</p></div><figure class="screenshot-frame"><a href="/images/freshness.png" target="_blank" rel="noopener" aria-label="Open the data freshness screenshot at full size"><img src="/images/freshness.png" width="1600" height="900" loading="lazy" alt="FM AI Assistent header showing loaded database counts, freshness state and Load data control" /></a><figcaption><span>The app exposes counts, freshness state and the manual Load data control.</span><a href="/images/freshness.png" target="_blank" rel="noopener">View full size ↗</a></figcaption></figure></section>
    <section class="section"><div class="section-heading"><div><p class="eyebrow">Accuracy boundaries</p><h2>Useful context still needs judgment.</h2></div><p>RAM decoding, save state and AI reasoning can all be incomplete or stale. Treat outputs as decision support, not authoritative game instructions.</p></div><div class="feature-grid"><article class="info-card"><h3>Game state changes</h3><p>A transfer, injury or contract change after the last load may not appear until the next refresh.</p></article><article class="info-card"><h3>Unknown values</h3><p>Prices, demands and sale proceeds that are not known remain unknown in decision tools.</p></article><article class="info-card"><h3>AI fallibility</h3><p>An assistant can misunderstand the question or overstate a conclusion. Verify IDs and values in the app and game.</p></article></div></section>
  </div><CallToAction />
</BaseLayout>
